  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "A note: counting 2-colourings of 3-regular hypergraphs with Pfaffian incidence graphs",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "A self-contained note (LaTeX, 10 pages) with an external-review package on counting the proper 2-colourings of 3-regular 3-uniform hypergraphs whose incidence graphs are Pfaffian. It states and proves, with pointers to the repository proofs: (A) on every connected non-2-colourable one, #col(H - L) is polynomial (Berman determinants over Robertson-Seymour-Thomas trisum trees, the trisum law); (B) with signed incidences counting stays polynomial unless a trisum square has three twisted branches (the junction similitude, multiplier alpha^2 + alpha beta + beta^2); (C) under signings it is #P-hard on Pfaffian graphs; (D) without signs it is #P-hard; (E) it is #P-hard on Pfaffian braces; plus: plain planar pages are always twisted, and the Fano plane is the only non-2-colourable one with a brace incidence graph. Every quoted number is reproduced by replay.py (the eleven cited checks rerun in a temporary copy) and the headline numbers by independent.py (fresh code). No new mathematical claim beyond the cited proofs.",
